> is x + y comutative for u8 x and y?
  note: read "comutative" as "commutative"
  note: commutative: it(x, y) = it(y, x) everywhere?
  ucas: it(x: u8, y: u8) = x + y
  ucas: lhs(x: u8, y: u8) = it(x, y)
  ucas: rhs(x: u8, y: u8) = it(y, x)
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (exhaustive)
> is x + y asociative for u8 x, y and z?
  note: read "asociative" as "associative"
  note: z is declared but not used here
  note: associative: it(it(a, b), c) = it(a, it(b, c)) everywhere?
  ucas: it(x: u8, y: u8) = x + y
  ucas: lhs(x: u8, y: u8, x3: u8) = it(it(x, y), x3)
  ucas: rhs(x: u8, y: u8, x3: u8) = it(x, it(y, x3))
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
  word-level ring identity: no AIG built, no SAT search (3 parameter(s), polynomial normal form over Z agrees mod 2^8)
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (proved by algebra (no SAT): word-level ring identity: both sides have the same polynomial normal form over Z in 3 parameter(s) mod 2^8; checked on 4096 sampled tuples (8 values per parameter))
> is x add ivite for u8 x?
  note: read "add ivite" as "additive"
  note: additive: it(a + b) = it(a) + it(b) everywhere?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: lhs(x: u8, x2: u8) = it(x + x2)
  ucas: rhs(x: u8, x2: u8) = it(x) + it(x2)
  ucas: equiv lhs rhs
lhs and rhs are equal on the domain of lhs (exhaustive)
> is x monotonik for u8 x?
  note: read "monotonik" as "monotonic"
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: monotonic it
monotonic it:
  strictly increasing on 0..255
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points (forward difference f(x+1) - f(x))
> is x injctive for u8 x?
  note: read "injctive" as "injective"
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: injective it
injective it:
  injective: yes (one-to-one)
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points
> is x surjctive for u8 x?
  note: read "surjctive" as "surjective"
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: surjective it
surjective it:
  surjective onto its type u8 (0..255): yes
  256 distinct values (proved, exhaustive over all 256 points)
> is x bijctive for u8 x?
  note: read "bijctive" as "bijective"
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x
  ucas: bijective it
bijective it:
  injective: yes (one-to-one)
  proved, exhaustive over all 256 points
  surjective onto its type u8 (0..255): yes
  256 distinct values (proved, exhaustive over all 256 points)
  bijective: yes
